        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 932,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 840,
        "paragraph_id": "1D08EA7C",
        "text": "Bed composition"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 33875,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 933,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 841,
        "paragraph_id": "7A1864E5",
        "text": "If the effect of different sediment fractions, sorting and armoring are of importance, a bed composition constituting multiple sediment fractions can be defined. Each sediment fraction is characterized by a median grain size (D50) and possible a D15 and D90 as well. When using multiple sediment fractions, multiple bed layers are needed as well to describe the vertical distribution of the sediment fractions in the bed."
      }
    ],
